WEBVTT

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.890
It's about time.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.850
What was that?

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.570
They've managed to awaken.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.590
Why aren't they forming ranks?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.490
The forest is in danger!

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.960
<b>The Boy from the West and the Knight of the Blue Storm</b>

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.300
I'll do it myself, Silver.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.560
Really, I can do it on my own.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.290
I'll be fine.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.180
What are you doing?

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.800
Oh, Elias.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.230
Good morning.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.890
Silky, wait, wait.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:33.930
I'm going to college soon, right?

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.250
So, I'm trying to get ready.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.160
Soon?

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.440
You mean in September?

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.820
You still have two more months.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:46.010
I apparently need to have
a uniform made first, though.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.600
My measurements...

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.710
Just let Silver do it.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.540
I know, but...

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.150
I want to get used to this hand.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.970
I was hoping to be more self-sufficient.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:07.990
Leave it to a professional. It'll be faster.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:08.780
Yeah.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.880
Thanks, Silky.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.260
What are you going to do with that?

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.400
I just need to send this to the college, 
and they'll send me a uniform.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.710
Are you upset that you don't get to make it?

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.500
S-Sorry, Silky.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.030
Those are the rules, apparently.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.550
Have you grown?

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.950
You were about this tall 
when you just got here.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.070
Was I?

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:41.340
Oh, you're right.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.810
I don't really feel taller.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.610
But...

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.220
I've gotten just a little closer to you.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.430
You're right.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.430
It's a bit like a sailor uniform.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.910
Sort of like the uniform 
I was wearing in Japan.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.480
I never thought I'd be 
wearing a uniform again.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.380
Come to think of it, I haven't 
asked you about school.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.140
I don't have that many 
good memories to share.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.560
I'm still a little scared,

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.010
but I'm excited to wear this uniform.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.260
Just a second.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.330
Thanks.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.830
Chise, your body's cold.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.770
You don't feel well, do you?

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:58.060
It seemed like you didn't get any sleep 
because of that thunder last night.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.180
Ah.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.830
That was definitely 
a vicious storm last night.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.410
Maybe I have a cold.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.250
Get some rest.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.690
You won't get better staying awake.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.060
Okay.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:41.180
<i>Last night's severe storm has 
stopped over central England.</i>

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.200
This, and this, and...

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.670
<i>The weather is predicted to 
remain unstable for some time.</i>

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:44.860
This.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:48.550
<i>Everyone should check to see if anything in their house got covered in dust.</i>

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.270
There.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:53.290
<i>Because we just had a storm...</i>

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.900
Oh! That, too.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.580
Okay,

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.890
that's everything.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.510
Are you telling me your
job is more important than mine?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.510
Would you stop shouting?

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:16.940
I'm exhausted from going back and 
forth to the hospital in London.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.990
Yeah, well, so am I.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.360
Damn it, this wouldn't be a problem 
if we lived in London proper...

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.970
Gabriel would have gotten 
worse if we'd stayed there.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.300
I know that!

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.500
I told you not to shout!

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.220
You're shouting louder!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.820
Fantastic, so we're even, then!

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:34.930
Fine.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.590
Man, it's rough.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.980
It's way more rural here than I thought.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.320
No, no.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.260
It's really just the middle of nowhere.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:00.830
I was hoping the scenery would at least 
be a bit more mystical, y'know?

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:04.780
Old forests, stone circles where giants 
would have shown up, stuff like that.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.230
There's none of it.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.270
Seriously, nothing mystical at all.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:13.460
I mean, I don't know this place, 
so I guess I can explore a bit.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.470
Yeah.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.930
I'm hiding from Mom and Dad.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.510
They're so annoying. I can't deal with them.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:25.380
Oh, yeah, I guess.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:29.210
The only thing that's better than London 
is the treehouse in the backyard.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.350
Yeah.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.920
There's a treehouse here.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.360
Come check it out, Oscar.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.830
This weekend, maybe?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.240
There are some historic sites nearby, too.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.690
We might find something weird.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.590
Like faeries, or haunted 
cemeteries, or something.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.970
Oh, okay.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.610
Nah, that's fair.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.380
Your mom and dad are busy.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:55.890
Yeah...

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.880
But you've gotta come
 over sometime, yeah?

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.680
At least once during the summer break.

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:00.890
Okay.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:02.020
Later.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.680
I'll call you.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:04.770
Bye-bye.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.530
Some journey this is...

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.710
You always do this when
you don't get your way.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.200
That's because you never listen to me.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.340
You're always just thinking about yourself.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.260
They're still at it.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:23.830
I'm thinking about this rationally!

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.090
Smoke?

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.190
Huh?

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.990
Maybe I'm seeing things.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.770
Wait, that's where lightning 
struck last night.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.610
No running!

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.610
Mom!

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.120
You were watching?

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:08.620
Are you going out?

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.140
Yeah, just going for a walk.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.460
Where's your medication?

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.430
I've got it.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.180
Keep it around your neck.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.590
I'm fine.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.020
It's for your own good.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.350
I'm not a kid anymore.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.840
If you aren't a kid, you 
ought to understand.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.810
I said, I'm fine!

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.880
What's her problem?

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.530
She drags me out to the countryside,

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:35.700
gets into fights, and blames
 it all on my sickness.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.710
Oh man, that's a record!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:38.790
Focus! Focus!

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:39.870
Seriously? Damn!

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.450
Damn!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.610
You've got this!

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.380
Go for world record!

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.680
It was around here, wasn't it?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.230
It's part of a stone circle!

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:11.960
It's chipped.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.490
It'll be pretty with a little polish.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.910
Crap, it's getting late.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.870
To think the Wild Hunt would 
have wandered so far...

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:17.510
I see.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.290
You've been separated from your master.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.280
Still cold, huh?

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.770
Yeah, a little.

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.970
Maybe you should rest a little longer.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:32.360
I think I've slept too much.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.620
Silver?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.160
Stay put.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:37.500
I'll go.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.340
How unusual.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.370
What's your business?

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.610
I merely brought a stray.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:52.960
What is this about?

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.910
This is per its request.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.720
I need to get back to the forest.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.600
Is something wrong with the forest?

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:02.720
The Wild Hunt woke up and trampled it.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.340
Wild Hunt?

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.320
Um...

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.950
Is something wrong?

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.870
You don't have to come out, Chise.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.940
She isn't dressed appropriately 
for the mid-summer.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:15.520
I've had chills since this morning.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.810
That, too, is the influence of 
the wandering Wild Hunt.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:22.990
They've lost their way, and 
are wandering this land.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.940
They're behaving differently than they should.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.040
Their steps are erratic.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.540
They wandered into the forest 
without forming ranks,

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.820
and trampled it.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.420
This one seems to have been 
separated from its master.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.720
What does that mean?

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:38.090
Look.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.830
The same thing is happening 
all over the forest.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:49.030
If this returns, it may bring 
order back to the Wild Hunt.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.220
I'll leave you to deal with it.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:54.100
I have my hands full taking 
care of the forest.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.520
Ask it to learn more.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.210
Well, then.

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:05.710
Come in.

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:11.090
Elias, what is the Wild Hunt?

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:13.340
I'll explain inside.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:18.800
Silky, tea and something 
with plenty of calories.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.730
There's a horse in the house.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:27.720
They are a band of knights 
that arrives with a storm

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:33.310
near the summer solstice every twenty 
or thirty seasons, to hunt horses.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.680
They leave death in their wake.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.120
Death?

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:41.110
Old branches and weeds are culled,

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:45.080
allowing for new branches 
and buds to emerge.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:49.190
Although it's not clear if that
is the Wild Hunt's original purpose.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:52.260
And this one was separated from that band?

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:53.830
That seems to be the case.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.920
Now, what should we do?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.090
How are we supposed to ask it anything?

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:01.860
Is there something you 
want to talk to us about?

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.040
Sorry, I don't understand.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.130
"I want to go home."

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.970
He said he wants to go home.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.420
You can understand, Ruth?

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:14.230
Kind of.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:17.300
Back when I was alive, I would talk 
to the horses on the farm sometimes.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.340
You're amazing, Ruth.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:22.230
Were you a sheep dog or something?

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:25.740
Ruth, please.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:26.560
Okay.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.280
Talk.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:33.810
"We were in a slumber.

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:39.090
We waited together with our 
friends inside a single boulder.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:43.560
When the time would come, we would 
run together to the promised land.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.670
Now was to be that time.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:53.150
Lightning split us apart, and I 
was separated from my friends.

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.090
I am their leader.

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:58.840
I must return.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:03.140
A knight and a horse 
together make up a leader.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:08.190
That knight... <i>My</i> knight... 
is nowhere to be found.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.030
Help me find my knight.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:17.260
Or else my friends will become night 
thieves, with no mind but to destroy the lands.

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:23.280
Once I am reunited with my 
knight, I will repay you."

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.910
You've gotten lost all by yourself, huh?

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.130
Lightning, eh?

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.890
Now we also know why you've been ill.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:36.380
So we need to find his knight, first.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.980
Chise, your body isn't stable yet.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.900
Promise me you'll be careful.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:43.880
Yes.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.430
This isn't good.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.520
I'm already getting chills again.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.580
Let's start tomorrow.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.010
You ought to lie down immediately.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.000
Okay.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.660
I don't think he can wait.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:02.230
Sorry, we'll leave in the morning.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.010
Okay.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:13.520
A well-polished stone bears power.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.640
That's what this book says, too.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.000
I might even be able to summon some spirits.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:32.710
There.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.040
Ow...

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.520
Was that my imagination?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.540
Wh-When did you get here?!

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:51.900
Who are you?

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:54.200
What are you doing here so late at night?

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:55.750
I'm lost.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.220
I have to go back.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.440
Y-You're lost?

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:02.310
Should I call the police?

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.220
Huh?

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.410
What's going on?

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:06.840
Is it busted?

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:09.310
Crap, it's Mom.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.620
Gabriel!

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:14.480
Are you all right? I heard a loud noise.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:18.280
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.240
Thank goodness.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:22.990
Um...

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:28.550
What's wrong with you?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.180
What are you doing up so late, anyway?

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.120
You've been polishing 
rocks again, haven't you?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.120
That's enough!

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.530
It's late!

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:39.690
We might not notice if 
something happens to you.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.930
<i>I'm the only one who can see him?</i>

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:44.930
Are you listening?!

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:46.720
Y-Yeah!

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.980
There's another storm coming, too.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:52.480
You know you tend to have your attacks 
when the weather's not good.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.560
I got it, Mom.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:55.930
Is that it?

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:58.070
I'll go back as soon as 
I'm done cleaning up.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.940
You can go back inside.

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:02.490
I'll wait until you're back in your room.

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.310
I can't leave my equipment here.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.200
I have to clean it up.

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:09.570
Five minutes.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:10.390
Got it.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.940
Go wait at the door, Mom.

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.200
I have an early morning, too.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.240
Hurry up.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.600
I got it.

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:24.720
You...

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:26.980
You're...

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:33.030
You're a spirit, aren't you?!

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.520
I-I don't know.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.550
Mom couldn't see you, though.

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:38.450
What kind of spirit?

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.220
The earth?

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.110
The wind?

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:42.000
Or an ancient god?

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:45.790
Oh man, I can't believe I get
 to meet a real spirit.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.760
I wonder if it's because 
I polished that rock.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.750
I-I don't know.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.600
I don't remember anything.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:56.100
Do you have amnesia?

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.810
But I have to get back.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.480
I have to get back...

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:07.850
Hey, should I help you?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.040
But in exchange, can you be my friend?

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.360
Friend?

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.990
What, you don't wanna?!

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.000
Uh, that's not it...

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.330
It's settled, then.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:22.440
I have to find out what kind 
of spirit you are, first.

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:25.450
I think it's around here somewhere...

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:26.490
That...

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:28.580
What's that rock?

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.780
Oh, this?

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.070
I picked it up today.

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:32.830
I'm still in the middle of polishing it.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.110
Wanna try touching it?

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:37.200
Okay.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.230
Did you remember something?

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:43.980
No.

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:45.090
Oh.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.020
Huh? Did something just...

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.450
Are you all right?

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.920
Hey, are you all right?

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:08.960
I'm okay.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:09.930
I'll be right there.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.730
Are you really okay?

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:13.430
Yeah.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:14.800
It happens all the time.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:18.530
I cough when I exercise or get excited.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.780
It's always "don't do this, 
don't do that"...

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:26.970
Even when I'm hanging out with friends, 
it's "don't run," "don't get dirty"...

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:30.070
But I'm the only one who can see you.

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:32.750
Mom wouldn't get angry at 
something she can't see.

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.190
I think we'll make good pals.

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:44.780
Do you always have that on you?

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:46.500
Just like me.

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:50.120
I keep this on my neck, too.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.430
Gabriel!

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:57.380
Are you done yet?

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.920
Crap, I have to go.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.880
You can sleep here.

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:05.190
Let's go find your home tomorrow.

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:07.370
I promise I'll find it.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:08.210
See ya!
